WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.313
Your two-minute presentation is ready.

00:00:02.313 --> 00:00:05.341
Then the producer says, we only have
ninety seconds.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:10.321
That change touches three places: the
brief in Gmail,

00:00:10.321 --> 00:00:13.786
the recordings in Dropbox, and the deck in
Google Slides.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:19.631
Here's the original cut: one minute,
fifty-six seconds.

00:00:19.631 --> 00:00:21.171
It fits the first brief.

00:00:21.171 --> 00:00:23.097
Now let's change the deadline.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:27.810
HardStop's model reads the new brief and
turns it into requirements.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.865
Each one links back to what the producer
actually wrote.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.536
The result must stay, with its explanation
and disclaimer.

00:00:37.536 --> 00:00:40.202
HardStop keeps those complete clips
together,

00:00:40.202 --> 00:00:42.750
removes the rollout, and checks the
timing.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:49.129
Here's the new version: eighty-six point
two seconds.

00:00:49.129 --> 00:00:51.587
That's the finished file's measured
length.

00:00:51.587 --> 00:00:53.016
Let's hear a few seconds.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.000
[Excerpt from the original recording]

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.801
It also copies the slide deck

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:02.734
and keeps exactly the slides that match
the video.

00:01:02.734 --> 00:01:04.553
The original deck stays intact.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:11.132
The video goes back to Dropbox, then gets
downloaded and checked.

00:01:11.132 --> 00:01:13.986
HardStop prepares this email draft for
review.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.712
Now ask for thirty seconds.

00:01:16.712 --> 00:01:19.876
The required recordings alone need almost
fifty-four.

00:01:19.876 --> 00:01:22.144
HardStop explains why they cannot fit,

00:01:22.144 --> 00:01:24.592
and leaves the working version untouched.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.196
You can write your own brief, too.

00:01:30.196 --> 00:01:31.553
The same checks apply.

00:01:31.553 --> 00:01:35.376
This example uses fictional content and
synthesized narration;

00:01:35.376 --> 00:01:38.089
the app calls and recorded results are
real.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:44.934
That's HardStop: change the brief, keep
the video and deck in step,

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:47.624
and know when the request simply cannot be
met.
